claude_session_archive__projects__-workspace-SuperGrok1-5__122b3aee-fa74-43c0-936d-39ff1eca854f.jsonl.txt:19452:@@REC4644|assistant|assistant|2026-06-10T00:02:28.984Z@@ [TOOL_USE Agent] {"subagent_type": "general-purpose", "description": "Fix batch F1: bindings + guards + tests", "model": "opus", "prompt": "Implement a precisely-specced fix batch in /workspace/SuperGrok1.5 (branch claude/h100-audit-maximal). Owner directives: no functionality suppressed; fixes activate/harden, never weaken. NO builds, NO GPU runs (a tuning fleet owns the GPU). AST-check every Python file you touch; keep C++ brace-balanced. A sibling agent owns csrc/fused/**, csrc/bindings/dispatch.cpp, grokking_optimizers/{dispatch.py,megakernel_codegen.py,megakernel_engine.py}, tests/hw/test_megakernel_vs_eager.py, decoder_oracle.py, decoder_kernel_mirror.py \u2014 DO NOT touch those. Another sibling owns grokking_race_v2.py and tuning/ \u2014 DO NOT touch those either.\n\nYOUR FILES: csrc/bindings/bindings.cpp, csrc/bindings/helpers.h, scripts/check_math_single_source.py, scripts/optimizer_math_manifest.json (regen only via the script), tests/hw/parity_gate_h100.py, tests/hw/test_reference_parity.py, grokking_optimizers/profile_maximal.py, grokking_optimizers/optimizers/{prodigy,looksam,muon,adamw,grokadamw,neuralgrok}.py (NOT supergrok*.py \u2014 recently rewired, leave them).\n\nFIXES (each cites its audit finding; implement exactly):\n1. [A2-H1] bindings.cpp `supergrok2_prepare_and_batched_step` (~line 2189-2226): add `check_params_grads(params, grads, \"supergrok2_prepare_and_batched_step\");` right after the `if (n == 0) return;` guard \u2014 mirroring its sibling `supergrok2_batched_step`.\n2. [A2-M1] helpers.h: add a variadic-ish secondary-list guard, e.g. `inline void check_list_len(const std::vector<torch::Tensor>& v, size_t expect, const char* what, const char* fn)` that TORCH_CHECKs `v.size()==expect` with a descriptive message. Then in bindings.cpp call it for EVERY secondary list in the multi-tensor bindings: grokadamw_fused_step (exp_avgs/exp_avg_sqs/emas), grokfast_fused_ema_adam_step, lion_fused_step (exp_avgs), neuralgrok_fused_step (exp_avgs/exp_avg_sqs + steps), prodigy_fused_step (exp_avgs/exp_avg_sqs/s_bufs/param_inits + steps), muon_fused_step (bufs), supergrok11_fused_step + supergrok15_fused_step (exp_avgs/exp_avg_sqs/mus/sharpness_cache + layer_alphas/layer_beta1s/steps \u2014 the scalar vectors via a size_t overload or a second helper), supergrok2_batched_step + supergrok2_prepare_and_batched_step (mus/slows/gru_states/sharpnesses + scalar vectors). Keep messages precise (which list, expected vs got).\n3. [A5-F6, C++ half only] bindings.cpp: define `constexpr int GROK_ABI_SCHEMA = 1;` near the PYBIND11_MODULE and expose `m.attr(\"__abi_schema__\") = GROK_ABI_SCHEMA;` with a comment block: bump on ANY exported-signature change; the Python-side check lands separately (dispatch.py is sibling-owned). This is additive and inert until the Python check exists \u2014 that is fine and stated in the comment.\n4. [A5-F4] scripts/check_math_single_source.py: add a `binding_regions` manifest section. Implement `_extract_function_body(src, fn_name)` (find `fn_name`'s signature line, walk braces to the matching close) + a `BINDING_FUNCS` tuple covering at least: supergrok11_fused_step, supergrok15_fused_step, supergrok2_batched_step, supergrok2_prepare_and_batched_step, grokadamw_fused_step, grokfast_fused_ema_adam_step, lion_fused_step, muon_fused_step, neuralgrok_fused_step, prodigy_fused_step. Hash each normalized body into the manifest under \"binding_regions\"; verify like the existing hashes; extend --update-manifest to regenerate. Then RUN `python scripts/check_math_single_source.py --update-manifest` (CPU-only) and verify the guard exits 0.\n5. [A5-F5] same script: harden the fused-consumer structural check \u2014 replace the adamw-only literal grep with a loop asserting `csrc/algorithms/<opt>.h` is included for ALL 11 opts, and FAIL LOUDLY (not skip) if the fused consumer file is missing/empty; additionally assert the consumer references each optimizer's apply symbol (grep for `<opt>_step` / `sg2_apply_step` call tokens) \u2014 if the sibling's in-flight opt_components.cuh refactor makes a specific symbol assertion fail, make THAT sub-check a clearly-labelled WARNING (not pass-silent, not hard-fail) so the guard stays usable mid-refactor, with a TODO to harden post-refactor.\n6. [A5-F7] tests/hw/test_reference_parity.py: `ref_sg_phi_forward` (~line 193-200) uses tanh; the canonical kernels use exact-erf GELU (supergrok11.h:50, supergrok15.h:47). Change to exact GELU (0.5*x*(1+erf(x/sqrt(2)))) and update its self-consistency tests to match. Do not touch ref_sg11_step/ref_sg2_apply_step math.\n7. [A5-F3] grokking_optimizers/profile_maximal.py Tier D: replace the inline jax Adam/Lion reimplementations as the \"math actually optimizes\" claim \u2014 import the fp64 reference steps from tests/hw/test_reference_parity.py (adamw + lion at minimum; more if trivial) and assert descent using THOSE; if importing the test module is awkward, move/duplicate nothing \u2014 add a tiny loader that imports it via importlib from the tests path with a comment. If that's genuinely infeasible without GPU/torch issues (torch IS importable here), then rename the tier's claim strings to \"reference-reimplementation sanity (does NOT validate shipped kernels)\" \u2014 prefer the real fix.\n8. [A3 trivials \u2014 optimizer files]:\n   a. prodigy.py: add state_dict/load_state_dict round-tripping _d_lr/_r_ema/_s_ema (the audit's 6-line pattern: stash under sd[\"_prodigy\"], pop+restore in load).\n   b. looksam.py: same pattern for _global_step (sd[\"_looksam\"]).\n   c. muon.py: constructor accepts a single iterable \u2014 `Muon(params, ...)` auto-splits by p.ndim==2 into the 2D/1D groups, preserving the existing explicit (params_2d, params_1d) path; docstring it.\n   d. adamw.py `_validate_grad`: add a device check \u2014 `if not g.is_cuda: raise RuntimeError(f\"...requires CUDA tensors; got CPU. GPU-only kernels, no CPU fallback.\")` (keep existing checks). Then make looksam/muon/neuralgrok/prodigy call `_validate_grad` (import it) at their step() grad-collection points so the CPU error is loud for them too.\n   e. grokadamw.py: the deprecated dead `gamma`/`decay` ctor args \u2014 keep accepting (back-compat) but emit a DeprecationWarning when a non-None/non-default value is passed, and say \"no kernel slot; ignored\".\n   f. neuralgrok.py: dead `inner_steps` arg \u2014 same DeprecationWarning treatment. Do NOT attempt the amplifier-gradient-path redesign here (separate task).\nValidation: python -m pytest tests/hw/test_reference_parity.py -m \"not hw\" -q must pass (CPU tests); check_math guard exit 0; AST checks. Report per-fix: file:line, what changed, test/guard results, anything you could not complete and why.", "run_in_background": true}
claude_session_archive__projects__-workspace-SuperGrok1-5__122b3aee-fa74-43c0-936d-39ff1eca854f.jsonl.txt:19459:@@REC4646|assistant|assistant|2026-06-10T00:03:19.725Z@@ [TOOL_USE Agent] {"subagent_type": "general-purpose", "description": "Fix batch F2: race + tuner + roofline", "model": "opus", "prompt": "Implement a precisely-specced fix batch in /workspace/SuperGrok1.5 (branch claude/h100-audit-maximal). Owner directives: no functionality suppressed; track race metrics every 10 steps; tuner metric = gradient steps to val-grok TEST-CONFIRMED. NO builds, NO GPU runs (a 30-process tuning+analysis fleet owns the GPU \u2014 your edits apply at the next fleet restart; do not kill anything). AST-check every Python file you touch.\n\nA sibling agent owns csrc/**, grokking_optimizers/{dispatch.py,megakernel_codegen.py,megakernel_engine.py}, tests/hw/test_megakernel_vs_eager.py + parity/test_reference files, profile_maximal.py, and optimizers/{prodigy,looksam,muon,adamw,grokadamw,neuralgrok}.py \u2014 DO NOT touch those. Another sibling owns the `_try_fused_step` function and the train_adamw/train_lion loop bodies inside grokking_race_v2.py \u2014 touch grokking_race_v2.py ONLY outside those regions.\n\nYOUR FILES: grokking_race_v2.py (outside the excluded regions), tuning/tune_optimizers.py, tuning/roofline.py.\n\nFIXES (each cites its audit finding; implement exactly):\n\n\u2014 grokking_race_v2.py \u2014\n1. [A4-H2] save_json's per-run dict (~lines 1334-1344): add `\"component_failures\": dict(getattr(r, \"component_failures\", {}) or {})` and `\"matmul_precision\": _resolve_matmul_precision(c)` [A4-M4]; also record `\"use_amp\": bool(c.get(\"use_amp\", False))`. Add `\"matmul_precision_default\": DEFAULT_CONFIG.get(\"matmul_precision\")` to the _meta block.\n2. [A4-H1] Patience reconciliation: argparse `--eval_every` default 100 \u2192 10 (the owner's every-10-steps directive \u2014 the current argparse default silently overrides DEFAULT_CONFIG's 10), and change `early_stop_patience` DEFAULT_CONFIG value 500 \u2192 50 with a comment: patience counts EVALS, so 50 evals \u00d7 eval_every=10 = 500-step post-grok hold; the old 500\u00d7100 exceeded max_steps and made the threshold stop unreachable (every race run burned the full budget).\n3. [A4-M3 spec] In _eval_log, when the stopper records the FIRST threshold crossing under val-stopping, also test-confirm: simplest faithful implementation \u2014 in `_fin`, set a new TrainResult field `grokking_step_test_confirmed` (add to __slots__/init): True iff r.grokking_step is not None AND, at the eval record nearest grokking_step, test_acc >= early_stop_threshold \u2212 0.05 (find via r.steps/r.test_accs); include it in save_json. Under test-stopping it's trivially True when grokked. Comment why (val-trained metas can fake-grok val).\n4. [A4-H3] Crash accounting: in the single-GPU `_run` exception path and the multi-GPU task exception path, instead of dropping the run, append a stub TrainResult with stopping_reason=f\"CRASHED: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\"[:300], total_steps=0, empty curves \u2014 AND make print_summary/plot paths tolerate empty-curve results (guard the np.mean/min over empty lists \u2014 skip crashed runs in curve plots but COUNT them in a new per-optimizer `crashes` field in the JSON summary + print a loud per-optimizer crash count). Grep every consumer of results lists (print_summary, plot_comparison, _interpolate_runs, _plot_full_sweep, save_json) and guard each against the stub (steps==[]).\n5. [A4-M6 config drift] Align in-code c.get defaults with OPTIMIZER_CONFIGS: train_supergrok's `supergrok_lamb` fallback 5.0 \u2192 1.0; train_neuralgrok's `neural_layers` fallback 3 \u2192 2; remove the dead `grokadamw_gamma`/`grokadamw_decay` c.get reads from train_grokadamw (constructor still accepts; race stops passing them) [A4-M7].\n6. [A4-M5 landmine] In the 9 non-whitelisted train loops (neuralgrok, grokadamw, supergrok, supergrok15, supergrok2, grokfast, muon, looksam, prodigy), the `if _try_fused_step(...): step += 1; continue` pattern would SKIP side-steps and _eval_log if those cells were ever whitelisted. Replace each with a loud guard comment + the safe structure: keep calling _try_fused_step where it is, but on True just fall through WITHOUT `continue` and WITHOUT re-running fwd/bwd? NO \u2014 these loops do fwd/bwd AFTER the fused attempt (the old L3 contract). The CORRECT minimal change per the new L1 contract: REMOVE the pre-forward `_try_fused_step` attempt + `continue` from these 9 loops entirely (it can never fire for them today, and its semantics are wrong for L1), leaving a one-line comment: \"L1 fused tail integration for this optimizer requires the adamw/lion post-backward structure (see train_adamw) \u2014 do not re-add the pre-forward continue pattern (it skips side-steps and eval).\" This removes dead-wrong code, not functionality.\n7. [A4-M1/M2 cosmetics] EarlyStopper: rename the step() parameter test_acc \u2192 metric_acc (update the two call sites in _eval_log), rename best_test_acc \u2192 best_metric_acc, and surface it: in _fin set r.final_... no \u2014 simplest: add `\"best_metric_acc\": st.best_metric_acc` via a TrainResult field set in _fin and include in save_json. Keep metric_name as-is.\n8. [A4-M8] Remove the dead `log_every` key from DEFAULT_CONFIG and the _common kwargs (grep all uses first; if anything reads it, leave and report instead).\n\n\u2014 tuning/tune_optimizers.py \u2014\n9. [A6-HIGH] mode_confirm: apply the SAME test-confirmation as the search objective \u2014 per confirm seed, grokked = (grokking_step is not None and final_test_acc >= 0.90); DNF score mirrors the objective's test-branch (CAP + (1\u2212final_test_acc)\u00b7CAP when val-grokked-but-unconfirmed, CAP + (1\u2212peak_val)\u00b7CAP otherwise); persist final_test_acc per seed in the winners JSON.\n10. [A6-HIGH] DNF shaping: objective's no-val-grok branch becomes `cap + (1.0 \u2212 max(out[\"peak_val_acc\"], 0.5 * out.get(\"peak_train_acc\", 0.0))) * cap` \u2014 requires run_trial_config to also return peak_train_acc (max of r.train_accs). Comment: gives TPE a gradient in the memorize-but-no-grok region.\n11. [A6-HIGH] Crash separation: in the objective's except branch, classify \u2014 if the exception message/type indicates infra (CUDA OOM 'out of memory', 'CUDA error', 'ABI', TypeError from the pybind boundary), re-raise as optuna.TrialPruned() (no score poisoning); only genuine config failures (everything else) get the crash score, and make that score carry gradient: `2*cap + (1.0 \u2212 last-known peak_val if available else 0.0) * 100`. Track peak_val via a mutable cell updated in cb.\n12. [A6 rec] n_startup_trials 8 \u2192 12 (both sampler and pruner); CONFIRM_SEEDS (1002, 1003) \u2192 (1002, 1003, 1004, 1005) and confirm top_k default 3 \u2192 5, winner by MEDIAN steps among configs grokking ALL confirm seeds (fall back: most seeds, then median). Update the module docstring.\n13. [A6-MED] mode_worker: add a startup orphan sweep \u2014 enumerate study.get_trials(deepcopy=False), for RUNNING trials older than 2 hours call storage set_trial_state_values to FAIL (wrap in try/except per trial, loud print). Comment the over-budget race as accepted-benign.\n14. [A6 fp16amp nit] Drop the inert `params[\"matmul_precision\"]=\"fp32\"` assignment in the fp16amp branch; comment that use_amp takes precedence in _autocast.\n15. [pruner intent] n_warmup_steps 999 \u2192 490 (first prunable rung at step 500) and dead_by for decoder/vit \u2192 cap*0.5 stays (mamba 6000 ok) \u2014 comment the effective first-prune step.\n\n\u2014 tuning/roofline.py \u2014\n16. [A6-HIGH] decoder seq bug: per-model seq map {decoder: 4 (hardcoded model build), vit: num_patches (16), mamba: 2*chain_length+2 (8)} \u2014 stop reading the unrelated seq_len key for decoder.\n17. [A6-HIGH] STATE_TENSORS: supergrok2 \u2192 9 (m,v,mu,slow,sharp + gru_hidden 4/elem) with the corrected derivation comment; re-derive the others from the optimizer sources and correct any that are off (grokfast: check its actual buffers; looksam m,v,sam_dir=3 \u2713; supergrok/15: m,v,mu,sharp=4 \u2713 \u2014 verify by reading each optimizer
